{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 660 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "5a5f251f2f895c572a258248a8f8c0eba079c285f0f533acf3b469c323ffd9f0" :edb/db-before-t 659 :edb/db-after-t 660 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533972 50 #inst "2026-10-05T22:29:26.716Z" 13194139533972 true] [17592186092108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275421 13194139533972 true] [17592186092108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275426 13194139533972 true] [17592186092109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275432 13194139533972 true] [17592186092113 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275408 13194139533972 true] [17592186092113 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275415 13194139533972 true] [17592186275408 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275409 13194139533972 true] [17592186275408 1089 "q-120831" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275408 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533972 true] [17592186275408 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{2}{5}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $1$ decimal place?" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275408 1113 #uuid "27d0bfd5-252f-58a2-8671-dfd467885e8d" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275408 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{2}{5})=0.411\\,516…≈0.411\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0.411\\,5$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.411\\,5.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.411\\,5.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.411\\,5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/ab3de51a23485b1776e014768b0775315694cd1147eb2772f71323d4d097dee2.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -0.411\\,5 \\\\  & ≈2.730\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈0.411\\,5\\cdot 2.730\\,1≈1.1,\n$$\n\nrounded to $1$ decimal place." 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275410 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275411 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275412 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275413 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275414 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1041 "selection" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275411 13194139533972 true] [17592186275409 1110 #uuid "5978ec59-872a-50fd-ab3f-d93edd808c2d" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275410 1034 "1.2" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275410 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275410 1111 #uuid "c9df5b26-cbd5-5a17-9996-b34a3fc56473" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275411 1034 "1.1" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275411 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275411 1111 #uuid "35f300b6-87e7-500b-93a9-480fc9785e72" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275412 1034 "1.3" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275412 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275412 1111 #uuid "ff8645aa-a0cf-52cb-869e-f3538acbfe43" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275413 1034 "3.1" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275413 1111 #uuid "7d7d5dd2-7d5f-5feb-bf0d-d1d7c1317419" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275414 1034 "2.1" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275414 1111 #uuid "70fa96d4-21ca-5555-abcb-67429b34cd97" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275415 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275416 13194139533972 true] [17592186275415 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275419 13194139533972 true] [17592186275415 1089 "q-331938" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275415 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533972 true] [17592186275415 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{3},$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$   are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}, $\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533972 true] [17592186275415 1113 #uuid "11dd0979-73bf-536a-b52c-17378c4b7ce9" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275415 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{2}{3})=-0.729\\,727…≈-0.7297\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-0.7297$ is not in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ To get the first solution that's within the required domain, we need to find an angle that's coterminal with $-0.7297.$ To do this, we simply add $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-0.7297+2\\pi ≈5.5535\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.7297.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/4a49f40b94a408ea0094eb9f8fd065622e2aad91e56c2eba24071442d0d32e4c.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.7297 \\\\  & ≈3.8713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈3.9,\\,x≈5.6.\n$$" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275417 13194139533972 true] [17592186275416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275418 13194139533972 true] [17592186275416 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533972 true] [17592186275416 1041 "field-1" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275416 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275417 13194139533972 true] [17592186275416 1110 #uuid "32648c8d-00f1-531e-96cd-6ac146373d0b" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275417 1034 "3.9" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275417 1111 #uuid "a7219c70-c22e-552a-a969-15b8ac036b96" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275418 1034 "3.8" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275418 1111 #uuid "bd3aa92e-4445-50fb-bad9-e9e21ece1c37" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275420 13194139533972 true] [17592186275419 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533972 true] [17592186275419 1041 "field-2" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275419 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275420 13194139533972 true] [17592186275419 1110 #uuid "a3ca7385-2c82-591c-9d95-d1ebbe288501" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275420 1034 "5.6" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275420 1111 #uuid "2f96d9ac-1505-5220-94fc-6517a09d1cef" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275421 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275422 13194139533972 true] [17592186275421 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275424 13194139533972 true] [17592186275421 1089 "q-332377" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275421 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533972 true] [17592186275421 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘},$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275421 1113 #uuid "65d13828-e711-5e04-8268-75cd05d3d258" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275421 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-{30}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ lies inside the domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{30}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={30}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/1b1a3d9a84ba0d6da8d5c2c21a91a6027b1b57e520be7c886ecf5da1a9de1ee0.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =X-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & ={210}^{∘}-{360}^{∘} \\\\  & =-{150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are:\n\n$$\nx=-{150}^{∘},\\,x=-{30}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275423 13194139533972 true] [17592186275422 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533972 true] [17592186275422 1041 "field-1" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275422 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275423 13194139533972 true] [17592186275422 1110 #uuid "b488967e-5cc0-58bc-9eb8-379983710841" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275423 1034 "-150" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275423 1111 #uuid "db41bb04-d31c-53bc-b850-081e17600da8" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275425 13194139533972 true] [17592186275424 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533972 true] [17592186275424 1041 "field-2" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275424 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275425 13194139533972 true] [17592186275424 1110 #uuid "036d78bd-2f45-567e-801a-d3ea340eb2de" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275425 1034 "-30" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275425 1111 #uuid "348ba320-4afc-5a66-82f2-62a2fd8ad60e" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275426 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275427 13194139533972 true] [17592186275426 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275430 13194139533972 true] [17592186275426 1089 "q-336322" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275426 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533972 true] [17592186275426 1100 "Expressed in **ascending order** in radians, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1=0,$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ are\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x≈$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533972 true] [17592186275426 1113 #uuid "0d66e8d7-a2af-5c95-a229-af9a46e09090" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275426 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{3})=-0.339\\,836…≈-0.3398\n$$\n\nSince $-0.3398$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.3398.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.3398.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.3398.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13970834/assets/ed9b300e3f4f79298feba6a2d61347d938ce64d7100ad7b0696e13dbe2a65238.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.3398 \\\\  & ≈3.4814\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & ≈3.4814-2\\pi ≈-2.8018\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx≈-2.8,\\,x≈-0.3.\n$$" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275427 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275428 13194139533972 true] [17592186275427 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275429 13194139533972 true] [17592186275427 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533972 true] [17592186275427 1041 "field-1" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275427 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275428 13194139533972 true] [17592186275427 1110 #uuid "129b1829-78a7-56bf-afc2-bfc95b6608fd" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275428 1034 "-2.8" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275428 1111 #uuid "8bd4a1d7-ff23-57d3-ba3d-60b1e5227d3c" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275429 1034 "2.8" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275429 1111 #uuid "bd465e0e-392a-5be9-9eb7-77867552c29c" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275431 13194139533972 true] [17592186275430 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533972 true] [17592186275430 1041 "field-2" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275430 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275431 13194139533972 true] [17592186275430 1110 #uuid "ce932f35-83c3-5a01-89bb-ab4d020b9137" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275431 1034 "-0.3" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275431 1111 #uuid "a11aba01-28c6-5362-8fa2-8ac3e880847f" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275432 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275433 13194139533972 true] [17592186275432 1089 "q-336511" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275432 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533972 true] [17592186275432 1100 "Find the exact solution to the equation  $2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\sqrt{2}=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$ Give your answer in degrees.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275432 1113 #uuid "d5095206-b0b3-51e4-b2b3-be06116f09b6" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275432 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\sqrt{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)={90}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${90}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={90}^{∘}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its maximum values at:\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\n$$\n\nSince the domain $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}$ is one period, and we have already found one maximum value in this period, we conclude that $x={90}^{∘}$ is the only solution." 13194139533972 true] [17592186275433 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275434 13194139533972 true] [17592186275433 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533972 true] [17592186275433 1041 "field-1" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275433 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275434 13194139533972 true] [17592186275433 1110 #uuid "755c8fdc-977e-5c20-ba7e-6da38c7287d4" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275434 1034 "90" 13194139533972 true] [17592186275434 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533972 true] [17592186275434 1111 #uuid "10f23361-57db-5978-a455-1b0d0f5390fe" 13194139533972 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-120831" 17592186275408 "q-120831/selection" 17592186275409 "q-120831/selection/336de2bb8f0e1e5bec5444214921ab4007f840558e694e1651575347e5aed4f7" 17592186275410 "q-120831/selection/4c51e084e6253614e5c4efd2c8489e6900ae5b8c4e1204f11752d4e103d95983" 17592186275411 "q-120831/selection/e983a3acef4246594c7c60522bdb0d85ed6924356b3a7dae378b4cc95ed4f927" 17592186275412 "q-120831/selection/eff549b88f0dad60b4aaf57a41812ed8f8a24b530f6b82e0efa8a15dca6852b6" 17592186275413 "q-120831/selection/f34afcd1d8d06e16f767da9737fea297f9b48d4af4bb29ac0a317e64a3a131e9" 17592186275414 "q-331938" 17592186275415 "q-331938/field-1" 17592186275416 "q-331938/field-1/9b6783aca2d6ef79b1d01f4b45f9cad932ac916cf5326206da9f4d74693258e8" 17592186275417 "q-331938/field-1/e69e46056c61d03ac81fa66e418618e77f184bfb88b9bbf8c04a941cc85eaec1" 17592186275418 "q-331938/field-2" 17592186275419 "q-331938